00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Richard III is a drama, war film directed by Richard Loncraine.

3
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
A murderous lust for the British throne sees Richard III descend into madness.

4
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Though the setting is transposed to the 1930s, England is torn by civil
war, split between the rivaling houses of York and Lancaster.

5
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Richard aspires to a fascist dictatorship, but must first remove the obstacles to his
ascension—among them his brother, his nephews and his brother's wife.

6
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
When the Duke of Buckingham deserts him, Richard's plans are compromised.

7
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Richard III, played by Ian McKellen.

8
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Queen Elizabeth, played by Annette Bening.

9
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
The Duke of Buckingham, played by Jim Broadbent.

10
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Earl Rivers, played by Robert Downey Jr..

11
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
Lady Anne, played by Kristin Scott Thomas.

12
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
James Tyrrell, played by Adrian Dunbar.

13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
Richard III is a 1995 film adaptation of William
Shakespeare's play of the same name.

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Directed by Richard Loncraine, the film adapts the play's story and characters to a setting based on
1930s Great Britain, with Richard depicted as a fascist plotting to usurp the throne.

15
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Ian McKellen portrays the title character, as well as
co-writing the screenplay with Loncraine.

16
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
The cast also includes Annette Bening as Queen Elizabeth, Jim
Broadbent as the Duke of Buckingham, Robert Downey Jr.

17
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
as Rivers, Kristin Scott Thomas as Anne Neville, Nigel Hawthorne as the Duke of Clarence, Maggie Smith as the Duchess of York, John Wood
as King Edward IV, Tim McInnerny as Sir William Catesby, and Dominic West (in his film debut) as Henry, Earl of Richmond.

18
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Richard III premiered in Brazil on 20 August 1995, and was released in the United States on 29
December 1995, and in the United Kingdom on 26 April of the following year.

19
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
While unsuccessful at the box office, it received
critical acclaim, and won several accolades.

20
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
At the 50th British Academy Film Awards, it won the awards for Best Production Design and Best Costume Design, with
nominations for Best British Film, Best Adapted Screenplay, and Best Actor in a Leading Role for McKellen.

21
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
It also earned Oscar nominations for Best Art Direction and Best Costume Design, and McKellen
was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Actor – Motion Picture Drama.

22
01:35:20,000 --> 01:35:26,000
The film explores themes of england, kidnapping, murder, king.

23
01:39:40,000 --> 01:39:46,000
The tone is emotional.
